sequenceDiagram
  actor Organizer
  actor Participant
  participant Host as Authorized event service
  participant DB as Persistent store
  participant Runtime as Owned runtime adapter
  Note over Host,DB: Local: persistent SQLite; cloud: selected Turso or DynamoDB
  Organizer->>Host: Prepare selected event problems
  Host->>Host: Validate event, team and runtime
  Host->>DB: Retain jobs and ownership
  alt New local Docker event
    Host-->>Organizer: Up to 512 dormant jobs prepared
    Participant->>Host: Start / resume own assigned problem
    Host->>Host: Check event/team access and active/memory limits
    Host->>DB: Persist owned operation and runtime ports
    Host->>Runtime: Create bounded Compose plan or resume existing project
    Runtime-->>Host: Outputs or failure
    Host->>DB: Persist status and private runtime data
    Participant->>Host: Stop (keep data)
    Host->>Runtime: Stop; retain writable layer and volumes, not RAM
    Host->>DB: Persist stopped status and retained runtime ports
  else Cloud AWS problem
    Host->>DB: Atomically retain owned deployment and dispatch outbox
    Host-->>Organizer: Accepted job reference
    Runtime->>DB: Dispatcher claims pending work
    Runtime->>Runtime: Step Functions invokes owned CloudFormation workers
    Runtime->>Runtime: Assume verified competitor role with required ExternalId
    Runtime->>DB: Persist progress, exact stack identity and terminal result
  else Native Cryptography Battle
    Host->>DB: Retain plugin identity and native state
    Host-->>Organizer: Ready without Docker or a competitor stack
  else Legacy local Docker event
    Host->>Runtime: Existing deployment lifecycle
    Runtime-->>Host: Outputs or failure
    Host->>DB: Persist status and private runtime data
  end
  Note over Host,Runtime: No automatic eviction or reset; synthetic allocation is not a Docker benchmark
  Note over Organizer,Runtime: Ordinary make destroy removes the AWS platform, default data and S3; external Turso is retained. Explicit --drain-events removes recorded competitor resources first.
